{"id":"w252228","name":"Poached Salmon with wild Huckleberries","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Poached_Salmon_with_wild_Huckleberries"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Poached_Salmon_with_wild_Huckleberries"},"image":"","cuisine":"Native American","country":"","region":"Americas","course":"main","protein":"seafood","diet":1,"allergens":32,"minutes":40,"time":{"prep":20,"cook":20,"passive":0,"passiveWhy":[]},"timeEstimated":true,"servings":"5","difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"item":"1 pound salmon fillet","qty":""},{"item":"1 cup fish stock","qty":""},{"item":"1 cup water","qty":""},{"item":"1 sprig fresh thyme","qty":""},{"item":"1 sprig fresh parsley","qty":""},{"item":"1 tbsp black peppercorns","qty":""},{"item":"½ cup huckleberries","qty":""},{"item":"1 lemon, sliced","qty":""}],"steps":["Preheat oven to 350°F.","In a baking dish, combine the fish stock and water. Add the salmon, making sure it is covered by liquid. If more liquid is needed, add equal parts water/fish stock until covered.","Add herbs, huckleberries, lemon slices, and peppercorns.","Place the in pan in the preheated oven, and bake for 15–18 minutes until salmon is flaky.","Serve and enjoy."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","lifestyle":127,"era":"modern"}